==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hwjuː/|/fjuː/|[ʍĭ̥ŭ̥]|[ɸĭ̥ŭ̥]}} <small>[very short and unvoiced]</small>
* {{audio|en|en-us-whew.ogg|Audio (GA)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uː|s=1}}
* {{homophone|en|phew}}

===Etymology 1===

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# An expressive sound made indicating the [[release]] of one's inner [[tension]]; the release of [[breath]]; an expression of [[relief]].
#: (from strenuous labour) {{ux|en|'''Whew!''' That box weighs a ton!}}
#: (from intense concern) {{ux|en|'''Whew!''' Thank goodness youʼre safe! I thought something terrible had happened to you!}}
#: (from fear of being seen) {{ux|en|'''Whew!''' That cop didnʼt see me! That was a close call!}}
# An expression of amazement or surprise.
#* {{quote-book|en|1981|[[w:P. L. Travers|P. L. Travers]]|[[w:Mary Poppins|''Mary Poppins'']]|edition=revised edition|chapter=1|text="...Now I must be off. '''Whew''', it's as cold as the North Pole. Which way is the wind blowing?"}}

